docs/PAYLOAD_CONTRACTS.md:186:- `temporal_status`: High-level anchoring state for the fact, currently `anchored`, `relative_only`, or `missing_anchor`.
docs/PAYLOAD_CONTRACTS.md:187:- `registry_version`: Canonical schema version for the temporal registry record family.
docs/PAYLOAD_CONTRACTS.md:189:- `start_time`, `end_time`, `granularity`, `is_approximate`, `is_range`, and `relative_markers`: First-class temporal fields duplicated from `temporal_context` for direct consumers.
docs/PAYLOAD_CONTRACTS.md:191:- `inference_mode`: Whether a relation or issue was derived from normalized temporal context or imported from an upstream contradiction workflow.
docs/PAYLOAD_CONTRACTS.md:193:- `inference_basis`: How a relation was derived. Current intake relations are inferred from normalized temporal context.
docs/PAYLOAD_CONTRACTS.md:194:- `issue_type`: Canonical temporal issue category, including registry-native categories such as `missing_anchor` and `relative_only_ordering` plus contradiction-derived temporal categories.
docs/PAYLOAD_CONTRACTS.md:198:Claim-support reasoning diagnostics may now include a claim-type-specific `temporal_rule_profile` when the system can evaluate chronology against an explicit legal timing frame.
